      "traceTextDiagram": "Symbol Extraction and Memory Store Indexing\n├── code_incremental_index skill entry \u003c-- skills/code_incremental_index/main.go:60\n│   ├── Open memory store \u003c-- 1a\n│   │   └── memory.Open() → SQLite connection \u003c-- internal/storage/memory/store.go:69\n│   ├── Extract symbols from file \u003c-- 1b\n│   │   └── extractSymbols() dispatcher \u003c-- skills/code_incremental_index/main.go:167\n│   │       └── Go AST extraction \u003c-- 1c\n│   │           └── extractor.Extract() \u003c-- skills/code_incremental_index/main.go:171\n│   └── Persist symbols loop \u003c-- skills/code_incremental_index/main.go:353\n│       └── for each symbol \u003c-- skills/code_incremental_index/main.go:353\n│           ├── Serialize to JSON \u003c-- 1d\n│           │   └── symbol.MarshalResult() \u003c-- skills/code_incremental_index/main.go:358\n│           ├── Save to store \u003c-- 1e\n│           │   └── store.Save() \u003c-- skills/code_incremental_index/main.go:374\n│           └── SQL upsert execution \u003c-- 1f\n│               └── INSERT...ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE \u003c-- internal/storage/memory/store.go:147\n└── Result: symbols indexed in memory.db",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen working with large codebases, developers need to quickly find relevant code without manually searching through thousands of files. The **symbol indexing system** solves this by automatically extracting and indexing code symbols (functions, classes, methods) whenever files are edited, enabling fast semantic code search.\n\nThe problem: Traditional text search (grep) finds keyword matches but doesn't understand code structure. You might search for \"authenticate\" and miss `AuthHandler.verify()` or `validateUser()`. The solution: **extract structured symbol metadata** (name, signature, documentation, location) and store it in a searchable database that understands code semantics.\n\n## Details\n\n### Architecture\n\nThe system uses **three SQLite databases**:\n- `memory.db` - stores indexed symbols [1f]\n- `embedding_queue.db` - queues symbols for vector embedding generation\n- Graph store - tracks code relationships (calls, imports)\n\n### Indexing Flow\n\nWhen a file is edited, the `code/incremental_index` skill triggers [1a]:\n\n1. **Open memory store** - Connects to SQLite database at `~/.foxctl/storage/memory.db` [1a]\n\n2. **Extract symbols** - Language-specific parsers extract code structure [1b]:\n   - Go: Uses AST parser to extract functions, methods, types [1c]\n   - Python/JS/TS: Regex-based extraction for classes and functions\n\n3. **Serialize** - Converts symbol metadata to JSON format [1d]:\n   ```go\n   {\n     \"symbol\": {\n       \"id\": \"file.go:FunctionName\",\n       \"name\": \"FunctionName\",\n       \"kind\": \"function\",\n       \"signature\": \"func FunctionName(arg string) error\",\n       \"file_path\": \"internal/pkg/file.go\",\n       \"start_line\": 42\n     }\n   }\n   ```\n\n4. **Persist** - Upserts into `named_memory` table [1e, 1f]:\n   - Entry name: `symbol://\u003cworkspace\u003e/\u003cfile\u003e:\u003csymbol_name\u003e`\n   - Uses `ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE` for idempotency\n   - Tracks workspace, session, timestamps\n\n### Key Design Decisions\n\n**Incremental indexing**: Only re-indexes changed files, not the entire codebase. This makes indexing fast enough to run on every file save.\n\n**Workspace isolation**: Symbols are scoped by workspace ID, allowing multiple projects to coexist without conflicts.\n\n**Deduplication**: Stale symbols are deleted when files are re-indexed [1e] - if a function is renamed or removed, the old entry is cleaned up.\n\n### Storage Schema\n\nThe `named_memory` table stores symbols with:\n- **name**: Unique identifier (e.g., `symbol://workspace/file.go:Handler`)\n- **type**: Always `\"symbol\"` for code symbols\n- **summary**: Symbol name for quick search\n- **result**: JSON blob with full metadata\n- **workspace**: Isolation boundary\n- **session_id**: Links to editing session\n\nThis indexed data powers the smart search system, which combines symbol search with semantic embeddings and text fallback to find relevant code."
    },
