      "traceTextDiagram": "Embedding Job Queue Enqueue Flow\n├── code_incremental_index skill\n│   ├── queueEmbeddings() invoked \u003c-- 2a\n│   └── embedding.OpenStore() \u003c-- 2b\n│       └── Opens embedding_queue.db \u003c-- internal/indexing/embedding/store.go:29\n├── store.Enqueue() called \u003c-- 2c\n│   ├── Begin transaction \u003c-- internal/indexing/embedding/store.go:110\n│   ├── For each symbol: \u003c-- internal/indexing/embedding/store.go:128\n│   │   ├── computeDigest(content) \u003c-- 2d\n│   │   ├── Check if exists query \u003c-- 2e\n│   │   │   └── SELECT EXISTS from symbol_embeddings\n│   │   └── stmt.ExecContext() insert \u003c-- 2f\n│   │       └── INSERT INTO embedding_jobs\n│   │           └── ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING\n│   └── Commit transaction \u003c-- internal/indexing/embedding/store.go:166\n└── Return EnqueueResult \u003c-- internal/indexing/embedding/store.go:170\n    └── {Queued, Skipped, JobIDs}",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nCode symbols (functions, classes, methods) need **semantic embeddings** to enable vector similarity search. Generating embeddings via external APIs (Voyage, Gemini) is slow and expensive, so the system uses a **background job queue** to process them asynchronously without blocking file indexing.\n\nWhen a file is indexed [2a], symbols are immediately stored in the memory database for fast keyword search, but embedding generation is deferred to a worker pool that processes jobs in priority order with automatic retries.\n\n## Details\n\n### Queue Database\n\nThe embedding queue uses a **separate SQLite database** (`embedding_queue.db`) [2b] from the main memory store. This isolation prevents embedding work from interfering with real-time symbol lookups.\n\n### Enqueue Process\n\nWhen symbols are queued [2c], the system:\n\n1. **Computes a SHA256 content digest** [2d] for each symbol's code\n2. **Checks if an embedding already exists** [2e] with the same digest to skip duplicate work\n3. **Inserts jobs into `embedding_jobs` table** [2f] with `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` for idempotency\n\nThe entire batch is wrapped in a **transaction** to ensure atomicity - either all symbols are queued or none are.\n\n### Deduplication Strategy\n\nContent digests enable **intelligent deduplication**: if a symbol's code hasn't changed, the system skips re-embedding it. This is critical for cost control since embedding APIs charge per token.\n\n### Job States\n\nJobs flow through states: `queued` → `running` → `ok` (or `error`/`retry`). The worker pool claims jobs atomically using `UPDATE...RETURNING` to prevent race conditions between concurrent workers.\n\n### Result Structure\n\nThe enqueue operation returns counts of **queued vs skipped symbols** [2a], allowing callers to track how much new work was created versus how much was deduplicated."
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "title": "Background Worker Embedding Generation",
      "description": "Part of the embedding worker system; background worker claims jobs, generates embeddings via API, and stores results",
      "locations": [
        {
          "id": "3a",
          "path": "internal/indexing/embedding/worker.go",
          "lineNumber": 163,
          "lineContent": "w.dispatchJobs(ctx, jobCh)",
          "title": "Dispatch Jobs",
          "description": "Dispatcher polls queue and sends jobs to worker pool"
        },
        {
          "id": "3b",
          "path": "internal/indexing/embedding/worker.go",
          "lineNumber": 172,
          "lineContent": "job, err := w.store.ClaimNext(ctx)",
          "title": "Claim Next Job",
          "description": "Atomically claims highest priority queued job for processing"
        },
        {
          "id": "3c",
          "path": "internal/indexing/embedding/store.go",
          "lineNumber": 180,
          "lineContent": "row := s.db.QueryRowContext(ctx, `\n\t\tUPDATE embedding_jobs\n\t\tSET state = 'running', updated_at = ?, attempts = attempts + 1\n\t\tWHERE id = (\n\t\t\tSELECT id FROM embedding_jobs\n\t\t\tWHERE state IN ('queued', 'retry')\n\t\t\tAND (scheduled_at IS NULL OR scheduled_at \u003c= ?)\n\t\t\tORDER BY priority DESC, created_at ASC\n\t\t\tLIMIT 1\n\t\t)\n\t\tRETURNING id, workspace_id, symbol_id, file_path, symbol_name, content,",
          "title": "Atomic Job Claim",
          "description": "Uses UPDATE...RETURNING to atomically claim job and prevent race conditions"
        },
        {
          "id": "3d",
          "path": "internal/indexing/embedding/worker.go",
          "lineNumber": 230,
          "lineContent": "embedding, err := w.provider.Embed(ctx, job.Content)",
          "title": "Generate Embedding",
          "description": "Calls external API (Voyage, Gemini, etc.) to generate embedding vector"
        },
        {
          "id": "3e",
          "path": "internal/indexing/embedding/worker.go",
          "lineNumber": 240,
          "lineContent": "if err := w.store.Complete(ctx, job.ID, embedding, w.provider.Model()); err != nil {",
          "title": "Store Embedding Result",
          "description": "Persists embedding vector and marks job as complete"
        },
        {
          "id": "3f",
          "path": "internal/indexing/embedding/store.go",
          "lineNumber": 235,
          "lineContent": "_, err = tx.ExecContext(ctx, `\n\t\tINSERT INTO symbol_embeddings\n\t\t\t(symbol_id, workspace_id, file_path, embedding, content_digest, model, dimensions, created_at)\n\t\tVALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\n\t\tON CONFLICT(workspace_id, symbol_id) DO UPDATE SET",
          "title": "Insert Embedding",
          "description": "Stores embedding vector as JSON blob in symbol_embeddings table"
        },
        {
          "id": "3g",
          "path": "internal/indexing/embedding/store.go",
          "lineNumber": 251,
          "lineContent": "_, err = tx.ExecContext(ctx, `\n\t\tUPDATE embedding_jobs\n\t\tSET state = 'ok', updated_at = ?, completed_at = ?, error = NULL\n\t\tWHERE id = ?\n\t`, nowStr, nowStr, jobID)",
          "title": "Mark Job Complete",
          "description": "Updates job state to 'ok' and records completion timestamp"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Background Embedding Worker System\n├── Worker Run Loop \u003c-- internal/indexing/embedding/worker.go:100\n│   ├── Ticker polls every 5s \u003c-- internal/indexing/embedding/worker.go:149\n│   │   └── dispatchJobs() \u003c-- 3a\n│   │       └── ClaimNext() from queue \u003c-- 3b\n│   │           └── UPDATE...RETURNING (atomic) \u003c-- 3c\n│   └── Worker goroutines (pool of 2) \u003c-- internal/indexing/embedding/worker.go:143\n│       └── processJob() \u003c-- internal/indexing/embedding/worker.go:212\n│           ├── Rate limiter wait \u003c-- internal/indexing/embedding/worker.go:227\n│           ├── provider.Embed() API call \u003c-- 3d\n│           └── store.Complete() \u003c-- 3e\n│               ├── Begin transaction \u003c-- internal/indexing/embedding/store.go:211\n│               ├── INSERT symbol_embeddings \u003c-- 3f\n│               └── UPDATE job state='ok' \u003c-- 3g\n└── Worker lifecycle\n    ├── Start() spawns goroutines \u003c-- internal/indexing/embedding/worker.go:84\n    └── Stop() graceful shutdown \u003c-- internal/indexing/embedding/worker.go:105",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nGenerating embeddings for code symbols is **expensive and slow**—each API call to services like Voyage or Gemini takes 100-500ms and costs money. When a developer edits a file containing 50 functions, you can't block the indexing process waiting for 50 sequential API calls (25+ seconds). The **background embedding worker system** solves this by decoupling embedding generation from symbol indexing: symbols are indexed immediately [1e], then queued for asynchronous embedding generation [2c], allowing the developer to continue working while embeddings are generated in the background.\n\n## Details\n\n### Architecture\n\nThe system uses a **persistent SQLite job queue** (`embedding_queue.db`) with two tables: `embedding_jobs` tracks work items with states (queued/running/ok/error), and `symbol_embeddings` stores the resulting vectors [3f]. This survives process restarts and provides durability.\n\n### Worker Pool\n\nA configurable pool of worker goroutines (default: 2) continuously polls the queue [3a]. The dispatcher claims jobs atomically using `UPDATE...RETURNING` [3c] to prevent race conditions—multiple workers can safely run concurrently without claiming the same job twice. Jobs are prioritized by priority level then creation time.\n\n### Processing Flow\n\nEach worker [3b]:\n1. **Rate limits** API calls (default: 5 requests/second) using a token bucket algorithm [3d]\n2. **Calls the embedding provider** (Voyage, Gemini, etc.) to generate the vector [3d]\n3. **Stores the result** in a transaction: inserts the embedding [3f] and marks the job complete [3g]\n\n### Retry Logic\n\nFailed jobs are automatically retried with **exponential backoff** (1min, 2min, 4min) up to 3 attempts. After max retries, jobs enter the 'error' state. This handles transient API failures gracefully.\n\n### Deduplication\n\nThe system computes a **SHA256 content digest** [2d] before enqueueing. If an embedding already exists with the same digest [2e], the job is skipped—avoiding redundant API calls when symbol content hasn't changed."
    },
