      "traceTextDiagram": "Smart Search Multi-Source Candidate Generation\n├── code_smart_search skill entry \u003c-- skills/code_smart_search/main.go:87\n│   ├── generateCandidates() \u003c-- 4a\n│   │   ├── memory.OpenWithConfig() \u003c-- 4b\n│   │   ├── retrieval.NewGenerator() \u003c-- 4c\n│   │   └── generator.Generate() \u003c-- 4d\n│   │       ├── searchSymbolIndex() \u003c-- 4e\n│   │       │   └── store.Search() queries symbols \u003c-- internal/retrieval/symbol_search.go:39\n│   │       ├── searchSemanticIndex() \u003c-- 4f\n│   │       │   └── embedProvider.Embed() + vector \u003c-- internal/retrieval/semantic_search.go:29\n│   │       ├── ripgrepFallback() \u003c-- 4g\n│   │       │   └── exec rg command for text search \u003c-- internal/retrieval/ripgrep.go:50\n│   │       └── mergeCandidates() \u003c-- 4h\n│   │           ├── apply source weights \u003c-- internal/retrieval/merge.go:35\n│   │           ├── deduplicate by path \u003c-- internal/retrieval/merge.go:22\n│   │           └── sort by final score \u003c-- internal/retrieval/merge.go:61\n│   └── return ranked candidates \u003c-- skills/code_smart_search/main.go:216\n└── invokeSnippetExtract() uses candidates \u003c-- skills/code_smart_search/main.go:143",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen developers ask questions like \"where is authentication handled?\" or \"how does the cache work?\", they need **relevant code snippets** from their workspace. The challenge is finding the right files among thousands without knowing exactly where to look.\n\nThe smart search system solves this by **combining three retrieval strategies**: searching an index of code symbols (functions, classes), performing semantic similarity search using embeddings, and falling back to text search with ripgrep. Each strategy has strengths—symbols are precise, embeddings understand meaning, ripgrep catches everything—so the system **merges results with weighted scoring** to surface the most relevant files.\n\n## Details\n\n### Multi-Source Candidate Generation\n\nThe entry point [4a] opens the memory store [4b] where indexed symbols and embeddings are stored, then creates a generator [4c] that orchestrates the search [4d].\n\n**Symbol search** [4e] queries the memory store for functions, classes, and methods whose names, signatures, or documentation match query tokens. This is fast and precise for direct references like \"find the `handleAuth` function.\"\n\n**Semantic search** [4f] generates an embedding vector for the user's question, then performs vector similarity search against stored symbol embeddings. This catches conceptual matches—asking about \"user login\" might find `authenticateUser()` even without exact keyword overlap.\n\n**Ripgrep fallback** [4g] runs when the first two sources return few results. It executes a text search across the workspace to ensure coverage, useful for finding string literals or comments.\n\n### Merging and Ranking\n\nThe merge step [4h] is critical: it **deduplicates candidates by file path** (the same file might appear from multiple sources), applies source-specific weights (symbols weighted 1.0, semantic 0.7, ripgrep 0.5), and adds a **multi-source bonus** when multiple strategies agree on the same file. Results are sorted by final score and limited to the top N candidates.\n\nThe ranked candidates are then passed to `code/snippet_extract` which reads the actual files and extracts relevant code snippets for the LLM to analyze."
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "title": "Symbol Index Search Implementation",
      "description": "Part of the retrieval system; searches memory store for symbols matching query tokens with BM25-like scoring",
      "locations": [
        {
          "id": "5a",
          "path": "internal/retrieval/symbol_search.go",
          "lineNumber": 39,
          "lineContent": "results, err := g.store.Search(ctx, workspaceID, term, queryLimit)",
          "title": "Query Memory Store",
          "description": "Searches memory store for symbol entries matching search term"
        },
        {
          "id": "5b",
          "path": "internal/storage/memory/store.go",
          "lineNumber": 566,
          "lineContent": "rows, err := s.db.QueryContext(ctx, `\n\t\tSELECT id, name, type, workspace, summary, result, digests, created_at, updated_at, last_accessed, access_count, session_id\n\t\tFROM named_memory\n\t\tWHERE workspace = ? AND (LOWER(name) LIKE ? OR LOWER(summary) LIKE ?)",
          "title": "SQL LIKE Search",
          "description": "Executes case-insensitive LIKE query on name and summary columns"
        },
        {
          "id": "5c",
          "path": "internal/retrieval/symbol_search.go",
          "lineNumber": 60,
          "lineContent": "res, err := symbol.UnmarshalResult(entry.Result)",
          "title": "Deserialize Symbol",
          "description": "Unmarshals JSON blob to extract symbol metadata"
        },
        {
          "id": "5d",
          "path": "internal/retrieval/symbol_search.go",
          "lineNumber": 80,
          "lineContent": "hits[i].score = scoreSymbol(hits[i].result.Symbol, qTokens)",
          "title": "Score Symbol",
          "description": "Computes relevance score based on token matches in name, signature, docs, file path"
        },
        {
          "id": "5e",
          "path": "internal/retrieval/symbol_search.go",
          "lineNumber": 114,
          "lineContent": "candidates = append(candidates, Candidate{\n\t\t\tPath:     sym.FilePath,\n\t\t\tSymbolID: sym.ID,\n\t\t\tName:     sym.Name,\n\t\t\tKind:     string(sym.Kind),\n\t\t\tScore:    hit.score / maxScore,",
          "title": "Build Candidates",
          "description": "Constructs candidate list with normalized scores and symbol metadata"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Symbol Index Search Flow\n├── searchSymbolIndex() entry point \u003c-- internal/retrieval/symbol_search.go:14\n│   ├── buildSearchTerms(question) \u003c-- internal/retrieval/symbol_search.go:19\n│   │   └── tokenize() extracts keywords \u003c-- internal/retrieval/symbol_search.go:138\n│   ├── for each search term \u003c-- internal/retrieval/symbol_search.go:34\n│   │   └── store.Search() query \u003c-- 5a\n│   │       └── SQL LIKE on name/summary \u003c-- 5b\n│   ├── for each result entry \u003c-- internal/retrieval/symbol_search.go:45\n│   │   └── symbol.UnmarshalResult() \u003c-- 5c\n│   ├── scoreSymbol() relevance scoring \u003c-- 5d\n│   │   ├── match on symbol name (5.0x) \u003c-- internal/retrieval/symbol_search.go:218\n│   │   ├── match on signature (1.0x) \u003c-- internal/retrieval/symbol_search.go:225\n│   │   ├── match on documentation (0.5x) \u003c-- internal/retrieval/symbol_search.go:230\n│   │   └── match on file path (0.3x) \u003c-- internal/retrieval/symbol_search.go:235\n│   ├── sort by score descending \u003c-- internal/retrieval/symbol_search.go:84\n│   └── build Candidate list \u003c-- 5e\n└── return ranked candidates \u003c-- internal/retrieval/symbol_search.go:126",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen developers ask questions like \"where is authentication handled?\" or \"find the database connection logic,\" the system needs to quickly search through thousands of code symbols (functions, classes, methods) to find relevant matches. **Symbol index search** solves this by maintaining a searchable index of all code symbols in the workspace, enabling fast retrieval based on natural language queries.\n\nThe challenge is matching fuzzy natural language questions to precise code symbol names. A query like \"user authentication\" should match symbols named `authenticateUser`, `UserAuth`, or `validateUserCredentials`, even though none contain the exact phrase.\n\n## Details\n\n### Query Processing\n\nThe search starts by **tokenizing the user's question** into keywords [5a], filtering out stop words and short tokens. For example, \"how does user authentication work?\" becomes `[\"user\", \"authentication\", \"work\"]`. These tokens are used to query the memory store using SQL LIKE patterns [5b].\n\n### Symbol Retrieval\n\nThe memory store contains serialized symbol entries stored as JSON blobs in a SQLite database. Each query returns matching entries, which are **deserialized back into symbol objects** [5c] containing metadata like name, signature, documentation, file path, and line numbers.\n\n### Relevance Scoring\n\nEach symbol is scored against the query tokens using a **weighted scoring algorithm** [5d]:\n- **Exact name matches get 5.0x weight** (highest priority)\n- Partial name matches get 2.0x weight\n- Signature matches get 1.0x weight\n- Documentation matches get 0.5x weight\n- File path matches get 0.3x weight\n\nThis ensures that a function named `authenticateUser` scores higher than one that merely mentions \"authentication\" in its documentation.\n\n### Result Ranking\n\nAfter scoring all matches, results are **sorted by score descending** and converted into a standardized `Candidate` structure [5e] containing the file path, symbol ID, name, kind (function/class/method), and normalized score (0-1 range). These candidates are then passed to downstream systems for snippet extraction or further processing."
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "title": "Semantic Search with Vector Embeddings",
      "description": "Part of the retrieval system; performs hybrid BM25 + vector similarity search using stored embeddings",
      "locations": [
        {
          "id": "6a",
          "path": "internal/retrieval/semantic_search.go",
          "lineNumber": 29,
          "lineContent": "vec, err := g.embedProvider.Embed(ctx, question)",
          "title": "Embed Query",
          "description": "Generates embedding vector for user's search question via API"
        },
        {
          "id": "6b",
          "path": "internal/retrieval/semantic_search.go",
          "lineNumber": 39,
          "lineContent": "results, err := searchable.SearchHybrid(ctx, question, queryVec, workspaceID, limit*2)",
          "title": "Hybrid Search",
          "description": "Combines BM25 lexical search with vector cosine similarity"
        },
        {
          "id": "6c",
          "path": "internal/storage/memory/search.go",
          "lineNumber": 243,
          "lineContent": "rawResults, err := ss.hybridSearcher.Search(\n\t\tctx,\n\t\tquery,\n\t\tqueryVector,\n\t\t\"named_memory\",\n\t\t\"name || ' ' || COALESCE(summary, '')\",",
          "title": "Execute Hybrid Search",
          "description": "Runs hybrid searcher on named_memory table with text and embedding columns"
        },
        {
          "id": "6d",
          "path": "internal/storage/memory/search.go",
          "lineNumber": 264,
          "lineContent": "entry, err := ss.Get(ctx, result.DocumentID, workspace)",
          "title": "Fetch Full Entry",
          "description": "Retrieves complete memory entry for each search result"
        },
        {
          "id": "6e",
          "path": "internal/retrieval/semantic_search.go",
          "lineNumber": 123,
          "lineContent": "candidates = append(candidates, Candidate{\n\t\t\tPath:     filePath,\n\t\t\tScore:    score,\n\t\t\tRawScore: r.Score,\n\t\t\tSource:   SourceSemantic,\n\t\t})",
          "title": "Build Semantic Candidates",
          "description": "Converts search results to candidates with semantic source tag"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Semantic Search with Vector Embeddings (Trace 6)\n├── Query Embedding Generation\n│   └── embedProvider.Embed(question) \u003c-- 6a\n│\n├── Hybrid Search Execution\n│   ├── SearchHybrid() entry \u003c-- 6b\n│   │   └── hybridSearcher.Search() \u003c-- 6c\n│   │       ├── BM25 lexical scoring \u003c-- internal/storage/memory/search.go:101\n│   │       ├── Vector cosine similarity \u003c-- internal/storage/memory/store.go:908\n│   │       └── Weighted score combination\n│   │\n│   └── Result Processing\n│       └── ss.Get(documentID) \u003c-- 6d\n│           └── Fetch full NamedEntry from DB \u003c-- internal/storage/memory/search.go:348\n│\n└── Candidate Construction\n    └── Build Candidate list \u003c-- 6e\n        └── Tag with SourceSemantic",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen developers search for code using natural language queries like \"authentication middleware\" or \"database connection pooling\", they need results that understand **semantic meaning**, not just keyword matches. A pure text search for \"auth\" might miss files about \"authentication\" or \"authorization\", while a symbol-only search might miss relevant implementation details in documentation or comments.\n\nThe **semantic search system** solves this by generating **vector embeddings** (numerical representations) of code symbols and using **cosine similarity** to find semantically related code, even when exact keywords don't match. This is combined with traditional **BM25 lexical search** in a hybrid approach that gets the best of both worlds: semantic understanding plus exact keyword matching.\n\n## Details\n\n### Query Embedding\nWhen a user asks a question, the system first converts it into a vector embedding by calling an external API (Voyage, Gemini, etc.) [6a]. This embedding captures the semantic meaning of the query in a high-dimensional space (typically 1024 dimensions).\n\n### Hybrid Search Strategy\nThe system performs **hybrid search** that combines two complementary approaches [6b][6c]:\n\n1. **BM25 scoring**: Traditional information retrieval that tokenizes the query and scores documents based on term frequency and inverse document frequency [search.go:101]\n2. **Vector similarity**: Computes cosine similarity between the query embedding and stored symbol embeddings [store.go:908]\n\nThe two scores are weighted and combined to produce a final relevance score. This hybrid approach outperforms either method alone because BM25 catches exact matches while vector search finds semantically similar code.\n\n### Result Retrieval\nFor each high-scoring result, the system fetches the complete `NamedEntry` from the memory store [6d], which contains the full symbol metadata including file path, symbol name, signature, and documentation [search.go:348].\n\n### Candidate Output\nResults are converted into `Candidate` objects tagged with `SourceSemantic` to distinguish them from symbol-index or ripgrep results [6e]. These candidates include normalized scores (0-1 range) and are later merged with candidates from other sources for final ranking.\n\n### Storage Architecture\nThe system stores embeddings as **JSON-encoded float32 arrays** in the `named_memory` table's `embedding` BLOB column. This allows semantic search without requiring a specialized vector database, though performance is limited compared to native vector indexes like those in Turso/LibSQL."
    },
    {
