        {
          "id": "7e",
          "path": "skills/code_smart_search/main.go",
          "lineNumber": 303,
          "lineContent": "return \u0026ExtractResult{\n\t\tFilesRelevant:   env.Data.Summary.FilesRelevant,\n\t\tSnippetsEmitted: env.Data.Summary.SnippetsEmitted,\n\t\tSnippetsInline:  env.Data.SnippetsInline,\n\t\tArtifact:        env.Data.Artifact,\n\t}",
          "title": "Return Snippets",
          "description": "Returns extracted code snippets with file paths, line numbers, and text content"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "code/smart_search skill execution \u003c-- skills/code_smart_search/main.go:86\n├── generateCandidates() orchestration \u003c-- skills/code_smart_search/main.go:91\n│   └── invokeSnippetExtract() \u003c-- 7a\n│       ├── Build candidate input JSON \u003c-- skills/code_smart_search/main.go:230\n│       │   └── map path + priority \u003c-- 7b\n│       ├── Spawn subprocess \u003c-- skills/code_smart_search/main.go:264\n│       │   └── exec foxctl run \u003c-- 7c\n│       │       └── code/snippet_extract skill \u003c-- skills/code_snippet_extract/main.go:86\n│       │           └── (reads files, extracts snippets)\n│       ├── Parse output envelope \u003c-- skills/code_smart_search/main.go:278\n│       │   └── json.Unmarshal \u003c-- 7d\n│       └── Return ExtractResult \u003c-- 7e\n│           ├── FilesRelevant count \u003c-- skills/code_smart_search/main.go:221\n│           ├── SnippetsEmitted count \u003c-- skills/code_smart_search/main.go:222\n│           ├── SnippetsInline (previews) \u003c-- skills/code_smart_search/main.go:223\n│           └── Artifact (full NDJSON) \u003c-- skills/code_smart_search/main.go:224\n└── Emit final output \u003c-- skills/code_smart_search/main.go:175\n    └── code/smart_search result",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen developers ask questions like \"where is authentication handled?\" or \"how does the payment flow work?\", they need **relevant code snippets** from the right files. The challenge: a codebase might have thousands of files, and traditional text search returns too many false positives. The **code/snippet_extract** subprocess solves this by taking a **ranked list of candidate files** (already filtered by upstream search) and extracting only the most relevant code snippets by reading the actual workspace files and applying intelligent filtering [7a].\n\nThis is the **final stage** of the smart search pipeline—after symbol indexing [1a], embedding generation [3a], and multi-source candidate ranking [4a] have identified promising files, snippet extraction reads those files and pulls out the specific functions, classes, or code blocks that answer the user's question.\n\n## Details\n\n**Input Processing**: The skill receives a JSON payload via stdin containing candidate file paths with priority scores [7b]. This avoids command-line length limits when dealing with many candidates.\n\n**Subprocess Execution**: Rather than being called as a library, code/snippet_extract runs as a **separate foxctl subprocess** [7c]. This provides process isolation and allows the skill to use the full foxctl runtime (path validation, artifact management, observability).\n\n**File Reading and Extraction**: The subprocess reads each candidate file from the workspace, respects size limits (64KB per file by default), and extracts relevant snippets by matching against query keywords. It handles symbol-targeted extraction (when a specific function/class is identified) and whole-file scanning.\n\n**Output Format**: Results are returned as a JSON envelope [7d] containing:\n- **SnippetsInline**: Truncated previews (512 bytes) for immediate display [7e]\n- **Artifact**: Full NDJSON file with complete snippet text, line numbers, and file paths\n- **Summary stats**: Files processed and snippets emitted counts\n\n**Why Subprocess?**: The subprocess architecture allows snippet_extract to be **reusable** across different entry points (smart_search, direct CLI invocation, other skills) while maintaining consistent path validation and security boundaries."
    }
  ],
  "description": "This codemap traces the complete flow from symbol extraction through embedding generation to smart code search. Key entry points: symbol indexing at [1a], embedding queue at [2a], worker processing at [3a], and smart search at [4a]. The system uses three SQLite databases: memory.db for symbols [1f], embedding_queue.db for jobs [2f], and supports hybrid search [6c].",
  "mermaidDiagram": "graph TB\n    subgraph SymbolIdx[\"Symbol Indexing\"]\n        style SymbolIdx fill:#fcc2d7\n        1a[\"1a: Open Memory Store\"]\n        1b[\"1b: Extract Symbols\"]\n        1c[\"1c: Go Symbol Extraction\"]\n        1d[\"1d: Serialize Symbol\"]\n        1e[\"1e: Persist Symbol Entry\"]\n        1f[\"1f: SQL Upsert\"]\n        \n        1a --\u003e 1b\n        1b --\u003e 1c\n        1c --\u003e 1d\n        1d --\u003e 1e\n        1e --\u003e 1f\n    end\n    \n    subgraph EmbedQueue[\"Embedding Queue\"]\n        style EmbedQueue fill:#fcc2d7\n        2a[\"2a: Queue Embeddings\"]\n        2b[\"2b: Open Embedding Store\"]\n        2c[\"2c: Enqueue Request\"]\n        2d[\"2d: Compute Content Digest\"]\n        2e[\"2e: Check Existing Embedding\"]\n        2f[\"2f: Insert Job\"]\n        \n        2a --\u003e 2b\n        2b --\u003e 2c\n        2c --\u003e 2d\n        2d --\u003e 2e\n        2e --\u003e 2f\n    end\n    \n    subgraph EmbedWorker[\"Embedding Worker\"]\n        style EmbedWorker fill:#ffec99\n        3a[\"3a: Dispatch Jobs\"]\n        3b[\"3b: Claim Next Job\"]\n        3c[\"3c: Atomic Job Claim\"]\n        3d[\"3d: Generate Embedding\"]\n        3e[\"3e: Store Embedding Result\"]\n        3f[\"3f: Insert Embedding\"]\n        3g[\"3g: Mark Job Complete\"]\n        \n        3a --\u003e 3b\n        3b --\u003e 3c\n        3c --\u003e 3d\n        3d --\u003e 3e\n        3e --\u003e 3f\n        3f --\u003e 3g\n    end\n    \n    subgraph SearchHub[\"Smart Search Generator\"]\n        style SearchHub fill:#a5d8ff\n        4a[\"4a: Generate Candidates\"]\n        4b[\"4b: Open Memory Store\"]\n        4c[\"4c: Create Generator\"]\n        4d[\"4d: Execute Generation\"]\n        4h[\"4h: Merge and Rank\"]\n        \n        4a --\u003e 4b\n        4b --\u003e 4c\n        4c --\u003e 4d\n    end\n    \n    subgraph SearchSources[\"Search Sources\"]\n        style SearchSources fill:#b2f2bb\n        4e[\"4e: Search Symbol Index\"]\n        4f[\"4f: Search Semantic Index\"]\n        4g[\"4g: Ripgrep Fallback\"]\n        \n        5a[\"5a: Query Memory Store\"]\n        5b[\"5b: SQL LIKE Search\"]\n        5c[\"5c: Deserialize Symbol\"]\n        5d[\"5d: Score Symbol\"]\n        5e[\"5e: Build Candidates\"]\n        \n        6a[\"6a: Embed Query\"]\n        6b[\"6b: Hybrid Search\"]\n        6c[\"6c: Execute Hybrid Search\"]\n        6d[\"6d: Fetch Full Entry\"]\n        6e[\"6e: Build Semantic Candidates\"]\n        \n        5a --\u003e 5b\n        5b --\u003e 5c\n        5c --\u003e 5d\n        5d --\u003e 5e\n        \n        6a --\u003e 6b\n        6b --\u003e 6c\n        6c --\u003e 6d\n        6d --\u003e 6e\n    end\n    \n    subgraph SnippetExt[\"Snippet Extraction\"]\n        style SnippetExt fill:#ffd8a8\n        7a[\"7a: Invoke Snippet Extract\"]\n        7b[\"7b: Build Extract Input\"]\n        7c[\"7c: Execute Subprocess\"]\n        7d[\"7d: Parse Envelope\"]\n        7e[\"7e: Return Snippets\"]\n        \n        7a --\u003e 7b\n        7b --\u003e 7c\n        7c --\u003e 7d\n        7d --\u003e 7e\n    end\n    \n    1f --\u003e|stores symbols| 5b\n    1e --\u003e|triggers| 2a\n    2f --\u003e|queues job| 3c\n    3f --\u003e|stores embeddings| 6c\n    \n    4d --\u003e|calls| 4e\n    4d --\u003e|calls| 4f\n    4d --\u003e|calls| 4g\n    \n    4e --\u003e|executes| 5a\n    4f --\u003e|executes| 6a\n    \n    5e --\u003e|merges into| 4h\n    6e --\u003e|merges into| 4h\n    \n    4h --\u003e|provides candidates| 7a"
}